"To find the distance from the origin to the point \\((-8,6)\\), we use the distance formula. The distance formula between two points \\((x_1, y_1)\\) and \\((x_2, y_2)\\) is given by:\n\n\\[\nd = \\sqrt{(x_2 - x_1)^2 + (y_2 - y_1)^2}\n\\]\n\nIn this case, the origin is \\((0,0)\\) and the point is \\((-8,6)\\). Plugging these coordinates into the formula, we get:\n\n\\[\nd = \\sqrt{((-8) - 0)^2 + (6 - 0)^2}\n\\]\n\n\\[\nd = \\sqrt{(-8)^2 + 6^2}\n\\]\n\n\\[\nd = \\sqrt{64 + 36}\n\\]\n\n\\[\nd = \\sqrt{100}\n\\]\n\n\\[\nd = 10\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the distance from the origin to the point \\((-8,6)\\) is \\(10\\) units.\n\n\\(\\boxed{10}\\)"
"To find the midpoint of a segment with endpoints \\((x_1, y_1)\\) and \\((x_2, y_2)\\), we use the midpoint formula:\n\n\\[\n\\left( \\frac{x_1 + x_2}{2}, \\frac{y_1 + y_2}{2} \\right)\n\\]\n\nGiven the endpoints \\((1, 4)\\) and \\((1, 10)\\), we substitute these coordinates into the formula:\n\n\\[\n\\left( \\frac{1 + 1}{2}, \\frac{4 + 10}{2} \\right)\n\\]\n\nSimplify the expressions:\n\n\\[\n\\left( \\frac{2}{2}, \\frac{14}{2} \\right) = (1, 7)\n\\]\n\nThe coordinates of the midpoint are \\((1, 7)\\). To find the sum of the coordinates, we add these coordinates together:\n\n\\[\n1 + 7 = 8\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the sum of the coordinates of the midpoint is \\boxed{8}.\n\nFinal Answer: The final answer is $8$. I hope it is correct."
"To find the area of kite \\(ABCD\\), we first need to determine the lengths of its diagonals. The diagonals of a kite are the line segments connecting opposite vertices.\n\n1. Calculate the length of diagonal \\(AC\\):\n\\[\nAC = \\sqrt{(12-0)^2 + (-2-7)^2} = \\sqrt{12^2 + (-9)^2} = \\sqrt{144 + 81} = \\sqrt{225} = 15\n\\]\n\n2. Calculate the length of diagonal \\(BD\\):\n\\[\nBD = \\sqrt{(7-1)^2 + (8-0)^2} = \\sqrt{6^2 + 8^2} = \\sqrt{36 + 64} = \\sqrt{100} = 10\n\\]\n\nThe area of a kite is given by half the product of its diagonals:\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 15 \\times 10 = 75\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the area of kite \\(ABCD\\) is \\(\\boxed{75}\\).}"
