"To simplify the expression \\(\\sqrt{\\sqrt[3]{\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{729}}}}\\), we will break it down step by step.\n\nFirst, simplify the innermost square root:\n\\[\n\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{729}} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{729}} = \\frac{1}{9}\n\\]\n\nNext, take the cube root of the result:\n\\[\n\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{1}{9}} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{9}} = \\frac{1}{3}\n\\]\n\nFinally, take the square root of the result:\n\\[\n\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{3}} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\n\\]\n\nTo rationalize the denominator, multiply the numerator and the denominator by \\(\\sqrt{3}\\):\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{3}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\n\\]\n\nThus, the simplified form of the expression is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}}\n\\]\n\nThis result has a rational denominator."
