"Let the weight of a single green ball be $g$ pounds and the weight of a single red ball be $r$ pounds.\n\nWe have the following system of equations:\n\n\\begin{align*}\n5g + 2r &= 10 \\\\\ng + 4r &= 7\n\\end{align*}\n\nWe can solve this system by elimination. First, we subtract the second equation from the first:\n\n\\begin{align*}\n(5g + 2r) - (g + 4r) &= 10 - 7 \\\\\n4g &= 3\n\\end{align*}\n\nNow, we substitute $g = \\frac{3}{4}$ back into the second equation:\n\n\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{3}{4} + 4r &= 7 \\\\\n4r &= 4 \\\\\nr &= 1\n\\end{align*}\n\nNow, we want to find the weight of $8$ red and $8$ green balls together. This is $8r + 8g = 8(1) + 8\\left(\\frac{3}{4}\\right) = 8 + 6 = \\boxed{14 \\text{ pounds}}$."
