"To solve the equation \\(\\frac{9-4x}{x+6}=7\\), we start by eliminating the fraction by multiplying both sides by \\(x+6\\):\n\n\\[\n9-4x = 7(x+6)\n\\]\n\nNext, we distribute the 7 on the right side:\n\n\\[\n9-4x = 7x + 42\n\\]\n\nNow, we isolate \\(x\\) by first moving all terms involving \\(x\\) to one side and constant terms to the other side. We do this by adding \\(4x\\) to both sides and subtracting 9 from both sides:\n\n\\[\n9 - 9 = 7x + 4x\n\\]\n\nSimplifying, we get:\n\n\\[\n0 = 11x + 42\n\\]\n\nSubtracting 42 from both sides:\n\n\\[\n-42 = 11x\n\\]\n\nFinally, we solve for \\(x\\) by dividing both sides by 11:\n\n\\[\nx = -4\n\\]\n\nThus, the solution to the equation is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{x = -4}\n\\]"
"To find the sum of all integers \\( x \\) for which \\( -30 \\leq x \\leq 26 \\), we can use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series. The sum of the first \\( n \\) integers is given by:\n\n\\[ S = \\frac{n(n + 1)}{2} \\]\n\nFirst, we need to determine the number of integers \\( n \\) in the range \\(-30\\) to \\(26\\). This can be found by subtracting the smallest integer from the largest integer and then adding 1:\n\n\\[ n = 26 - (-30) + 1 = 26 + 30 + 1 = 57 \\]\n\nNow, we can find the sum of these integers:\n\n\\[ S = \\frac{57(57 + 1)}{2} = \\frac{57 \\times 58}{2} = \\frac{3366}{2} = 1713 \\]\n\nTherefore, the sum of all integers \\( x \\) for which \\( -30 \\leq x \\leq 26 \\) is \\( \\boxed{1713} \\)."
"For the quadratic equation \\(3x^2 + 7x + c = 0\\) to have two real roots, the discriminant must be non-negative. The discriminant \\(\\Delta\\) of a quadratic equation \\(ax^2 + bx + c = 0\\) is given by \\(\\Delta = b^2 - 4ac\\).\n\nHere, \\(a = 3\\), \\(b = 7\\), and \\(c = c\\). Therefore, the discriminant is:\n\\[\n\\Delta = 7^2 - 4 \\cdot 3 \\cdot c = 49 - 12c\n\\]\n\nFor the discriminant to be non-negative, we need:\n\\[\n49 - 12c \\geq 0\n\\]\n\\[\n49 \\geq 12c\n\\]\n\\[\n\\frac{7}{4} \\geq c\n\\]\n\nThe positive integer values of \\(c\\) that satisfy this inequality are \\(c = 1, 2, 3, 4\\).\n\nThe product of these values is:\n\\[\n1 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 4 = 24\n\\]\n\nSolution: 24"
