"To evaluate the expression \\((x + y)(x - y)\\) when \\(x = 15\\) and \\(y = 5\\), we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Substitute \\(x = 15\\) and \\(y = 5\\) into the expression \\((x + y)(x - y)\\).\n2. Simplify the expression step by step.\n\nFirst, substitute \\(x = 15\\) and \\(y = 5\\) into the expression:\n\n\\[\n(x + y)(x - y) = (15 + 5)(15 - 5)\n\\]\n\nNext, simplify inside the parentheses:\n\n\\[\n15 + 5 = 20\n\\]\n\\[\n15 - 5 = 10\n\\]\n\nNow, multiply the results together:\n\n\\[\n20 \\times 10 = 200\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\((x + y)(x - y)\\) when \\(x = 15\\) and \\(y = 5\\) is \\(\\boxed{200}\\).\n\nFinal Answer: The final answer is 200."
"To solve the problem, we need to evaluate the expression \\(6 \\star 5\\) using the given operation \\(\\star\\), which is defined as \\(K \\star L = (K + L)(K - L)\\).\n\nStep 1: Identify the values of \\(K\\) and \\(L\\) in the expression \\(6 \\star 5\\).\nHere, \\(K = 6\\) and \\(L = 5\\).\n\nStep 2: Substitute \\(K\\) and \\(L\\) into the operation definition.\n\\[6 \\star 5 = (6 + 5)(6 - 5)\\]\n\nStep 3: Simplify the expression inside the parentheses.\n\\[6 + 5 = 11\\]\n\\[6 - 5 = 1\\]\nSo, the expression becomes:\n\\[6 \\star 5 = 11 \\cdot 1\\]\n\nStep 4: Perform the multiplication.\n\\[11 \\cdot 1 = 11\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\(6 \\star 5\\) is \\(\\boxed{11}\\).\n\nFinal Answer: The final answer is \\(11\\). I hope it is correct."
