"To find the value of \\(\\frac{2x^3 - 3y^2}{6}\\) given \\(x = 3\\) and \\(y = 2\\), we will follow these steps:\n\n1. Substitute the values of \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) into the expression.\n2. Simplify the expression.\n\nFirst, substitute \\(x = 3\\) and \\(y = 2\\) into the expression:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{2(3)^3 - 3(2)^2}{6}\n\\]\n\nNext, calculate the values inside the numerator:\n\n\\[\n2(3)^3 = 2 \\cdot 27 = 54\n\\]\n\\[\n3(2)^2 = 3 \\cdot 4 = 12\n\\]\n\nNow, substitute these values back into the expression:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{54 - 12}{6}\n\\]\n\nSimplify the numerator:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{42}{6}\n\\]\n\nFinally, divide 42 by 6:\n\n\\[\n7\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of the expression is \\(\\boxed{7}\\)."
"The given series is a geometric series with the first term \\(a = \\frac{1}{2}\\) and common ratio \\(r = \\frac{1}{2}\\). The number of terms \\(n\\) is 10. The sum \\(S\\) of the first \\(n\\) terms of a geometric series is given by the formula:\n\n\\[ S = a \\frac{1-r^n}{1-r} \\]\n\nSubstituting the given values:\n\n\\[ S = \\frac{1}{2} \\frac{1-\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^{10}}{1-\\frac{1}{2}} \\]\n\nSimplify inside the fraction:\n\n\\[ S = \\frac{1}{2} \\frac{1-\\frac{1}{1024}}{\\frac{1}{2}} = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{1023}{1024} \\cdot 2 = \\frac{1023}{1024} \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of the series expressed as a common fraction is:\n\n\\[ \\boxed{\\frac{1023}{1024}} \\]"
"To find \\( t(f(-2)) \\), we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate \\( f(-2) \\).\n2. Use the result from step 1 to find \\( t(f(-2)) \\).\n\n**Step 1: Calculate \\( f(-2) \\).**\n\nThe function \\( f(x) \\) is given by \\( f(x) = x^2 - 3 \\).\n\n\\[\nf(-2) = (-2)^2 - 3 = 4 - 3 = 1\n\\]\n\n**Step 2: Use the result from step 1 to find \\( t(f(-2)) \\).**\n\nThe function \\( t(x) \\) is given by \\( t(x) = 9 + 2f(x) \\).\n\n\\[\nt(f(-2)) = 9 + 2f(-2)\n\\]\n\nSubstitute \\( f(-2) = 1 \\):\n\n\\[\nt(f(-2)) = 9 + 2 \\cdot 1 = 9 + 2 = 11\n\\]\n\nTherefore, \\( t(f(-2)) \\) is \\(\\boxed{11}\\)."
