"First, we need to evaluate \\(\\lceil (3.6)^2 \\rceil\\).\n\n\\[\n(3.6)^2 = 12.96\n\\]\n\nThe ceiling function \\(\\lceil x \\rceil\\) gives the smallest integer greater than or equal to \\(x\\). Therefore,\n\n\\[\n\\lceil 12.96 \\rceil = 13\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to evaluate \\(\\lceil 3.6 \\rceil\\).\n\n\\[\n\\lceil 3.6 \\rceil = 4\n\\]\n\nNow, we need to evaluate \\(( \\lceil 3.6 \\rceil )^2\\).\n\n\\[\n( \\lceil 3.6 \\rceil )^2 = 4^2 = 16\n\\]\n\nFinally, we subtract the second result from the first:\n\n\\[\n\\lceil (3.6)^2 \\rceil - ( \\lceil 3.6 \\rceil )^2 = 13 - 16 = -3\n\\]\n\nThus, the answer is\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{-3}\n\\]"
"To find the value of \\(4 * 3\\) given the operation \\(a * b = 2a + 3b\\), we need to substitute \\(a = 4\\) and \\(b = 3\\) into the operation formula.\n\nStep 1: Identify the values of \\(a\\) and \\(b\\).\n\\[ a = 4 \\]\n\\[ b = 3 \\]\n\nStep 2: Substitute \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) into the operation formula \\(a * b = 2a + 3b\\).\n\\[ 4 * 3 = 2(4) + 3(3) \\]\n\nStep 3: Perform the multiplications.\n\\[ 2(4) = 8 \\]\n\\[ 3(3) = 9 \\]\n\nStep 4: Add the results of the multiplications.\n\\[ 8 + 9 = 17 \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\(4 * 3\\) is \\(\\boxed{17}\\)."
"We start with the given equation:\n\\[ f^{-1}(x+4) = 2f^{-1}(x) + 1 \\]\n\nFirst, let's find \\( f^{-1}(17) \\). We can express \\( f^{-1}(17) \\) in terms of \\( f^{-1}(5) \\):\n\\[ f^{-1}(17) = f^{-1}(5 + 4) \\]\n\nUsing the given equation:\n\\[ f^{-1}(5 + 4) = 2f^{-1}(5) + 1 \\]\n\nLet \\( y = f^{-1}(5) \\). Then:\n\\[ f^{-1}(17) = 2y + 1 \\]\n\nWe know that \\( f^{-1}(5) = 2 \\) because \\( f(2) = 5 \\). Therefore:\n\\[ f^{-1}(17) = 2(2) + 1 \\]\n\\[ f^{-1}(17) = 4 + 1 \\]\n\\[ f^{-1}(17) = 5 \\]\n\nThus, the solution is \\( \\boxed{5} \\)."
