"To evaluate \\(\\left(\\frac{i}{4}\\right)^4\\), we can use the property of complex numbers and exponents. Recall that \\(i\\) is the imaginary unit, where \\(i^2 = -1\\).\n\nFirst, let's rewrite the expression:\n\\[\n\\left(\\frac{i}{4}\\right)^4 = \\frac{i^4}{4^4}\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate \\(i^4\\):\n\\[\ni^4 = (i^2)^2 = (-1)^2 = -1\n\\]\n\nNow, we calculate \\(4^4\\):\n\\[\n4^4 = 256\n\\]\n\nSo, we substitute these values back into the expression:\n\\[\n\\frac{i^4}{4^4} = \\frac{-1}{256}\n\\]\n\nFinally, we simplify the fraction:\n\\[\n\\frac{-1}{256} = -\\frac{1}{256}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\(\\left(\\frac{i}{4}\\right)^4\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-\\frac{1}{256}}\n\\]"
