"To find the 5th term of the geometric sequence, we first need to determine the common ratio \\( r \\). The 7th term of a geometric sequence with first term \\( a \\) and common ratio \\( r \\) is given by:\n\n\\[ a \\cdot r^6 = 5103 \\]\n\nGiven that the first term \\( a \\) is 7, we have:\n\n\\[ 7 \\cdot r^6 = 5103 \\]\n\nSolving for \\( r^6 \\):\n\n\\[ r^6 = \\frac{5103}{7} = 729 \\]\n\nTaking the sixth root of both sides:\n\n\\[ r = \\sqrt[6]{729} = 3 \\]\n\nNow that we have the common ratio \\( r \\), we can find the 5th term of the sequence. The 5th term is given by:\n\n\\[ a \\cdot r^4 = 7 \\cdot 3^4 = 7 \\cdot 81 = 567 \\]\n\nTherefore, the 5th term is:\n\n\\[ \\boxed{567} \\]"
