"To solve the system of equations for \\( c \\), we start by substituting the expressions for \\( b \\) and \\( d \\) into the first equation.\n\nGiven:\n\\[ a - b = 2(c + d) \\]\n\\[ b = a - 2 \\]\n\\[ d = c + 5 \\]\n\nSubstitute \\( b = a - 2 \\) and \\( d = c + 5 \\) into the first equation:\n\\[ a - (a - 2) = 2(c + (c + 5)) \\]\n\nSimplify the left side:\n\\[ a - a + 2 = 2(c + c + 5) \\]\n\\[ 2 = 2c + 10 \\]\n\nNow, solve for \\( c \\):\n\\[ 2 = 2c + 10 \\]\n\\[ 2 - 10 = 2c \\]\n\\[ -8 = 2c \\]\n\\[ c = -4 \\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( c \\) is:\n\\[ c = -4 \\]\n\nFinal Answer: The final answer is \\(-4\\). I hope it is correct."
