"To find the number of 3-letter words that contain the letter A at least once, we can use the principle of complementary counting. First, we calculate the total number of possible 3-letter words without any restrictions. Each position can be any of the 26 letters, so the total number of 3-letter words is:\n\n\\[ 26^3 = 17576 \\]\n\nNext, we calculate the number of 3-letter words that do not contain the letter A at all. For each position, there are 25 possible letters (since A is not allowed). Therefore, the number of 3-letter words without A is:\n\n\\[ 25^3 = 15625 \\]\n\nThe number of 3-letter words that contain the letter A at least once is the total number of 3-letter words minus the number of 3-letter words without A:\n\n\\[ 17576 - 15625 = 1951 \\]\n\nThus, the number of 3-letter words that satisfy the condition of containing the letter A at least once is:\n\n\\[ \\boxed{1951} \\]"
