"To determine the number of congruent segments needed for Figure 25, we need to observe the pattern in the sequence. Each figure contains one more triangle than the preceding figure. Let's denote the number of triangles in the \\( n \\)-th figure as \\( T_n \\).\n\nFrom the problem, we know:\n- Figure 1 has \\( T_1 = 1 \\) triangle.\n- Figure 2 has \\( T_2 = 2 \\) triangles.\n- Figure 3 has \\( T_3 = 3 \\) triangles.\n- Figure 4 has \\( T_4 = 4 \\) triangles.\n\nWe can see that the number of triangles in the \\( n \\)-th figure is given by the formula:\n\\[ T_n = \\frac{n(n+1)}{2} \\]\n\nFor Figure 25:\n\\[ T_{25} = \\frac{25(25+1)}{2} = \\frac{25 \\times 26}{2} = \\frac{650}{2} = 325 \\]\n\nThus, the number of congruent segments needed to make Figure 25 is \\(\\boxed{325}\\)."
